---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import {
  SYSTEM_METRICS,
  STM32_PINOUT,
  BOM_ITEMS,
  FIRMWARE_MODULES,
  BUILD_SESSIONS,
  SAMPLE_FLIGHT_DATA
} from '../data/ignisData';
---

<Layout title="Project IGNIS — Open-Source Rocket Avionics, TVC & Active Fin Stabilization">
  <Header />

  <!-- HERO SECTION -->
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-top-meta">
        <span class="badge badge-accent">OPEN-SOURCE ROCKETRY AVIONICS</span>
        <span class="badge badge-blue">STM32G473VET6 • 170 MHz CORTEX-M4F</span>
        <span class="badge badge-green">100 Hz COMPLEMENTARY + PID + 4-FIN X-MIX</span>
        <span class="badge badge-amber">3-CHANNEL MOSFET PYRO & DUAL NVM</span>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-left">
          <div class="hero-kicker mono">WHY MODEL ROCKETS NEED ACTIVE CONTROL // PROJECT IGNIS</div>
          <h1 class="hero-title">
            MAKE ROCKETS FLY <span class="accent-text">STRAIGHT.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Traditional model rockets rely on passive fins that turn into crosswinds and veer off-course. <strong>Project IGNIS</strong> is a complete open-source avionics platform that actively steers model rockets using <strong>real-time 100 Hz thrust vectoring (TVC)</strong> and <strong>4-fin X-configuration aerodynamic surfaces</strong> powered by an <strong>STM32G473VET6</strong> flight computer.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-cta-row">
            <a href="#why-needed" class="btn btn-primary">THE MISSION &amp; WHY →</a>
            <a href="#fin-simulator" class="btn">ANIMATED FIN SIMULATOR</a>
            <a href="#mission-timeline" class="btn">FLIGHT STAGING (T-0 TO T+45s)</a>
            <a href="#telemetry-replayer" class="btn">LIVE FLIGHT REPLAYER</a>
            <a href="#studio-3d" class="btn">3D HARDWARE STUDIO</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-right panel">
          <div class="panel-bar">
            <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.74rem;color:var(--accent);">IGNIS-CORE 3D PCBA • HARDWARE ROTATION</span>
            <span class="badge badge-green">VERIFIED KICAD EXPORT</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-pcb-preview">
            <img src="/renders/ignis-core-3d-iso.png" alt="IGNIS-CORE STM32G473VET6 Flight Computer 3D PCB" />
          </div>
          <div class="hero-pcb-caption mono">
            <span>U3: STM32G473VET6</span>
            <span>U7: MPU-6500</span>
            <span>U8: MS5611</span>
            <span>U10: Ra-02 LoRa</span>
            <span>Q1–Q3: IRLZ44N / IRF520</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- KEY METRICS STRIP -->
      <div class="metrics-grid">
        {SYSTEM_METRICS.map((m) => (
          <div class="metric-card panel">
            <span class="metric-label">{m.label}</span>
            <div class="metric-value">{m.value}</div>
            <span class="metric-sub">{m.sub}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 00. THE GENESIS, INSPIRATION & WHY THIS PROJECT EXISTS -->
  <section id="why-needed" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <span class="section-index">00 // THE MISSION, INSPIRATION &amp; PROBLEM STATEMENT</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Why Model Rockets Crash &amp; Why We Built Project IGNIS</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-desc">
          The engineering motivation: from the aerodynamic flaws of passive model rocketry to the benchtop disasters and breakthroughs that created IGNIS.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="why-grid">
        <!-- The Problem -->
        <div class="panel story-card">
          <div class="story-badge">
            <span class="badge badge-red">THE CURSE OF PASSIVE STABILITY</span>
          </div>
          <h3>1. The "Weathercocking" Problem</h3>
          <p>
            For 70 years, model rocketry has relied entirely on <em>passive aerodynamic stability</em>: ensuring the Center of Pressure (CP) sits behind the Center of Mass (CM). But passive fins have a fatal flaw: <strong>when a horizontal crosswind strikes the rocket, aerodynamic lift on the tail rotates the vehicle INTO the wind.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            Instead of flying straight up to space, the rocket arcs sideways, burns propellant horizontally at 300 km/h, and crashes into trees, power lines, or distant fields. Without active steering, every launch in a 10-knot breeze is a roll of the dice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- The Inspiration -->
        <div class="panel story-card">
          <div class="story-badge">
            <span class="badge badge-accent">INSPIRATION &amp; VISION</span>
          </div>
          <h3>2. Orbital Technology for Amateur Rockets</h3>
          <p>
            Modern orbital rockets don't rely on passive stability. <strong>SpaceX's Falcon 9</strong> and <strong>Starship</strong> steer actively using gimbaled rocket engines (TVC) during ascent and deploy aerodynamic grid fins and steerable body flaps to stabilize through supersonic and subsonic atmospheric descent.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pioneered in amateur rocketry by innovators like <strong>Joe Barnard (BPS.space)</strong>, active thrust vectoring proved that model rockets can fly vertically and land autonomously. But existing commercial hardware was either closed-source, cost over $500, or relied on fragile hobby dev boards. <strong>IGNIS was born to make active GNC 100% open-source, affordable, and reproducible.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Why Drones Failed -->
        <div class="panel story-card">
          <div class="story-badge">
            <span class="badge badge-amber">THE SILICON BREAKTHROUGH</span>
          </div>
          <h3>3. Why Drone Flight Controllers Can't Fly Rockets</h3>
          <p>
            Many makers try putting Betaflight or ArduPilot drone controllers on a rocket. <strong>They fail immediately:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="story-list">
            <li><strong>Propellers vs. Fins:</strong> Drones steer by varying the RPM of 4 spinning electric motors. Rockets steer with pulsed PWM servos pushing aerodynamic fins or a gimbaled motor mount against solid motor exhaust.</li>
            <li><strong>High-G Saturation:</strong> Drone gyros and accelerometers saturate and clip at 16g during rocket launch, causing the attitude filter to instantly lose orientation.</li>
            <li><strong>No Pyrotechnics:</strong> Drone boards have zero high-current MOSFET stages to fire electric matches for parachute ejection at apogee.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- The Solution: TVC + Active Fins -->
        <div class="panel story-card">
          <div class="story-badge">
            <span class="badge badge-green">THE IGNIS ARCHITECTURE</span>
          </div>
          <h3>4. Hybrid TVC + Coast-Phase Aerodynamic Fins</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Thrust Vector Control (TVC) only works while the motor is burning</strong> (typically 1.5 to 2.5 seconds on solid composite motors). Once the motor burns out, TVC is completely powerless!
          </p>
          <p>
            Project IGNIS solves this by implementing an <strong>X-configuration 4-fin aerodynamic mixing system</strong>. During the high-speed coast phase (2.5s to 8.2s up to apogee), our 100 Hz PID controller continues to actively deflect the 4 fins, damping roll and holding the vehicle locked to vertical until peak altitude.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 01. INTERACTIVE 3D WEBGL STUDIO -->
  <section id="studio-3d" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <span class="section-index">01 // INTERACTIVE 3D WEBGL HARDWARE &amp; AIRFRAME STUDIO</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Explore the Flight Computer &amp; Airframe in 3D Space</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Interact with populated 3D PCBA models (with 3D STEP components) and parametric FreeCAD airframe assemblies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="studio-layout panel">
        <div class="studio-toolbar">
          <div class="model-tabs">
            <button type="button" class="btn model-tab active" data-src="/models/ignis-core-pcb.glb" data-title="IGNIS-CORE Flight Computer PCBA (STM32G473VET6)" data-meta="KiCad 3D Export • 71 Components • LQFP-100 + Ra-02 LoRa + MPU-6500 + MS5611 + IRLZ44N">
              1. IGNIS-CORE PCBA (.GLB)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn model-tab" data-src="/models/datalogger-pcb.glb" data-title="Auxiliary Blackbox Data Logger PCBA (ATmega328P + Dual 24LC1025)" data-meta="KiCad 3D Export • TQFP-32 ATmega328P + 2× 24LC1025 EEPROM + DS1337S+ RTC">
              2. Aux Data Logger PCBA (.GLB)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn model-tab" data-src="/models/AvionicsBay.gltf" data-title="Modular Avionics Bay Sled & Enclosure Assembly" data-meta="FreeCAD Assembly • Internal Shock-Damped Sled & Core Mounting Frame">
              3. Avionics Bay (.GLTF)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn model-tab" data-src="/models/Rocket.gltf" data-title="Complete IGNIS Active-Controlled Rocket Airframe" data-meta="FreeCAD Full Airframe • Nose Cone, Payload Bay, Avionics Bay & Fin Can">
              4. Full Rocket Assembly (.GLTF)
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="camera-controls">
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="cam-iso">ISO VIEW</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="cam-top">TOP VIEW</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="cam-side">SIDE VIEW</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="toggle-rot">AUTO-ROTATE: ON</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="viewer-stage">
          <model-viewer
            id="ignis-3d-viewer"
            src="/models/ignis-core-pcb.glb"
            alt="IGNIS 3D Hardware Model"
            auto-rotate
            camera-controls
            shadow-intensity="1"
            exposure="1.1"
            interaction-prompt="none"
          ></model-viewer>
        </div>

        <div class="studio-footer">
          <div>
            <strong id="viewer-model-title" class="mono">IGNIS-CORE Flight Computer PCBA (STM32G473VET6)</strong>
            <p id="viewer-model-meta" class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem;color:var(--text-muted);">
              KiCad 3D Export • 71 Components • LQFP-100 + Ra-02 LoRa + MPU-6500 + MS5611 + IRLZ44N
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.74rem;color:var(--text-secondary);">
            [LMB + DRAG] ORBIT • [SCROLL] ZOOM • [RMB + DRAG] PAN
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02. ANIMATED X-FIN PHYSICS & PID SIMULATOR (THE FINS MOVE!) -->
  <section id="fin-simulator" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <span class="section-index">02 // REAL-TIME GNC ATTITUDE CONTROL &amp; FIN KINEMATICS</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Interactive 100 Hz PID &amp; Dynamic Moving Fin Simulator</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Drag the attitude error sliders or click <strong>Trigger Wind Gust</strong> to watch the 4 fin blades physically pivot in real time and see the restoring aerodynamic lift vectors calculated by the <code>Flight.c</code> autopilot.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sim-grid">
        <!-- Controls Panel -->
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="sub-header">
            <span class="badge badge-accent">AUTOPILOT CONTROLS</span>
            <h3>Attitude Perturbation &amp; Autopilot Mode</h3>
          </div>

          <div class="mode-row">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="sim-arm-btn" data-armed="1">
              STATE: ARMED (ACTIVE PID CONTROL)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="sim-gust-btn" style="border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent);">
              💨 TRIGGER WIND GUST (DEMO)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="sim-reset-btn">
              CENTER / ZERO
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="led-indicator-box" id="sim-led-box">
            <span class="led-dot" id="sim-led-dot" style="background:#ef4444;box-shadow:0 0 12px #ef4444;"></span>
            <div>
              <div class="mono" id="sim-led-title" style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:700;">PB9 WS2812B: SOLID RED (255, 0, 0) — ARMED</div>
              <div class="mono" style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--text-muted);">TIM4_CH4 + DMA1_CH1 (800 kHz Pulse Train Actively Streaming)</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="slider-group">
            <div class="slider-label">
              <span>Filtered Pitch Angle Error (<code>θ</code>)</span>
              <strong class="mono" id="val-pitch">+10.0°</strong>
            </div>
            <input type="range" id="slider-pitch" min="-30" max="30" step="0.5" value="10" />
          </div>

          <div class="slider-group">
            <div class="slider-label">
              <span>Filtered Roll Angle Error (<code>ϕ</code>)</span>
              <strong class="mono" id="val-roll">-8.0°</strong>
            </div>
            <input type="range" id="slider-roll" min="-30" max="30" step="0.5" value="-8" />
          </div>

          <div class="slider-group">
            <div class="slider-label">
              <span>Gyro Yaw Angular Rate (<code>ω_z</code>)</span>
              <strong class="mono" id="val-yaw">+15.0 °/s</strong>
            </div>
            <input type="range" id="slider-yaw" min="-60" max="60" step="1" value="15" />
          </div>

          <div class="pid-readout-grid mono">
            <div class="pid-box">
              <span>PID PITCH CMD</span>
              <strong id="out-pitch-cmd">-12.00</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="pid-box">
              <span>PID ROLL CMD</span>
              <strong id="out-roll-cmd">+9.60</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="pid-box">
              <span>PID YAW CMD</span>
              <strong id="out-yaw-cmd">-9.00</strong>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Dynamic Visual Moving Fins Panel -->
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="sub-header">
            <span class="badge badge-green">3D WEBGL DYNAMICS &amp; AERODYNAMIC FORCES</span>
            <h3>Real-Time 3D Rocket Fin Kinematics &amp; Lift Vectors</h3>
          </div>

          <!-- Configuration & Camera Toolbar -->
          <div class="fin-stage-toolbar mono">
            <div class="toolbar-group">
              <span class="toolbar-label">AERO CONFIG:</span>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-xs cfg-btn active" id="btn-cfg-x">X-CONFIG (45°/135°/225°/315°)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-xs cfg-btn" id="btn-cfg-plus">CRUCIFORM + (0°/90°/180°/270°)</button>
            </div>
            <div class="toolbar-group">
              <span class="toolbar-label">CAMERA:</span>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-xs cam-btn active" id="btn-cam-orbit">3D ORBIT</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-xs cam-btn" id="btn-cam-side">SIDE (PITCH)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-xs cam-btn" id="btn-cam-aft">AFT BASE (RADIAL)</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-xs" id="btn-toggle-flow">AIRFLOW: ON</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="xfin-interactive-stage">
            <!-- 3D Three.js WebGL Stage -->
            <div class="three-stage-wrap">
              <canvas id="three-fin-canvas"></canvas>
              <div class="canvas-hint mono">[LMB + DRAG] 3D Orbit • [SCROLL] Zoom • [RMB + DRAG] Pan</div>
              <div class="canvas-overlay-legend mono">
                <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:#f59e0b;"></span><span>LIFT FORCE VECTORS (PERPENDICULAR TO CHORD)</span></div>
                <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:#06b6d4;"></span><span>AIRFLOW STREAMLINES (DOWNWARD V_INF)</span></div>
                <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:#ffffff;"></span><span>RADIAL HINGE PIVOT AXES (SPANWISE)</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Fin Angles & Pulse Width Readout Cards -->
            <div class="fin-angle-cards">
              <div class="fin-card">
                <div class="fin-card-top mono">
                  <span style="color:var(--accent);" id="fin1-title">FIN 1: QUADRANT I (45° • PA0/TIM2_CH1)</span>
                  <strong id="fin1-angle-badge">90° (1500 µs)</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="fin-bar-track"><div class="fin-bar-fill" id="fin1-bar" style="width:50%;background:var(--accent);"></div></div>
                <div class="fin-card-sub mono">
                  <small>Deflection: <span id="fin1-deflect-deg">0.0°</span></small>
                  <small id="fin1-mix-formula">-0.71·P - 0.71·Y + R</small>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="fin-card">
                <div class="fin-card-top mono">
                  <span style="color:var(--blue);" id="fin2-title">FIN 2: QUADRANT II (135° • PA1/TIM2_CH2)</span>
                  <strong id="fin2-angle-badge">90° (1500 µs)</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="fin-bar-track"><div class="fin-bar-fill" id="fin2-bar" style="width:50%;background:var(--blue);"></div></div>
                <div class="fin-card-sub mono">
                  <small>Deflection: <span id="fin2-deflect-deg">0.0°</span></small>
                  <small id="fin2-mix-formula">+0.71·P - 0.71·Y + R</small>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="fin-card">
                <div class="fin-card-top mono">
                  <span style="color:var(--green);" id="fin3-title">FIN 3: QUADRANT III (225° • PA2/TIM2_CH3)</span>
                  <strong id="fin3-angle-badge">90° (1500 µs)</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="fin-bar-track"><div class="fin-bar-fill" id="fin3-bar" style="width:50%;background:var(--green);"></div></div>
                <div class="fin-card-sub mono">
                  <small>Deflection: <span id="fin3-deflect-deg">0.0°</span></small>
                  <small id="fin3-mix-formula">+0.71·P + 0.71·Y + R</small>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="fin-card">
                <div class="fin-card-top mono">
                  <span style="color:var(--amber);" id="fin4-title">FIN 4: QUADRANT IV (315° • PA3/TIM2_CH4)</span>
                  <strong id="fin4-angle-badge">90° (1500 µs)</strong>
                </div>
                <div class="fin-bar-track"><div class="fin-bar-fill" id="fin4-bar" style="width:50%;background:var(--amber);"></div></div>
                <div class="fin-card-sub mono">
                  <small>Deflection: <span id="fin4-deflect-deg">0.0°</span></small>
                  <small id="fin4-mix-formula">-0.71·P + 0.71·Y + R</small>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Mathematical Physics Explainer Strip -->
          <div class="matrix-explainer-box mono" style="margin-top:1rem;">
            <strong>AERODYNAMIC RIGOR: WHY DRONE MIXERS FAIL ON ROCKETS</strong>
            <p style="font-size:0.75rem;margin:0.35rem 0 0;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.5;">
              • <strong>True Radial Pivot Axis:</strong> Each fin rotates on an outward spanwise shaft perpendicular to the airframe centerline. Deflection changes angle of attack <code>α</code> to the oncoming air, generating lift perpendicular to the chord.<br />
              • <strong>Pure Roll Damping:</strong> All 4 fins share an identical <code>+Roll</code> sign (like a windmill/propeller). If signs were mixed (+ − − + like a quadcopter), roll moments would cancel each other out.<br />
              • <strong>Orthogonal Pitch &amp; Yaw:</strong> In 45° X-config, <code>Pitch</code> creates equal and opposite couples on diagonal pairs without inducing roll or yaw: <code>[−P, +P, +P, −P]</code> dot <code>[+R, +R, +R, +R] = 0</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Live USB Telemetry Broadcast -->
          <div class="usb-frame-box mono" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
            <span class="usb-frame-label">STREAMING USB CDC CSV FRAME (PA11/PA12 @ 100 Hz):</span>
            <code id="sim-csv-line">10.00,-8.00,15.00,-12.00,9.60,-9.00,81,79,84,118,1</code>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03. INTERACTIVE 5-STAGE FLIGHT PROFILE & STAGING WALKTHROUGH -->
  <section id="mission-timeline" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div>
          <span class="section-index">03 // FLIGHT PHASES &amp; PYROTECHNIC SEQUENCING</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Interactive Flight Profile: From Pad (T-0) to Recovery (T+45s)</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Click each flight phase below to inspect the avionics state machine, pyro firing triggers, and sensor transitions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mission-layout panel">
        <!-- Phase Tabs -->
        <div class="phase-tabs">
          <button type="button" class="btn phase-tab active" data-phase="0">
            PHASE 1: PAD STANDBY (T-0s)
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn phase-tab" data-phase="1">
            PHASE 2: MOTOR BOOST (T+0s – T+2.5s)
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn phase-tab" data-phase="2">
            PHASE 3: COAST &amp; FIN DAMPING (T+2.5s – T+8.2s)
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn phase-tab" data-phase="3">
            PHASE 4: APOGEE &amp; CHUTE PYRO (T+8.2s)
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn phase-tab" data-phase="4">
            PHASE 5: DESCENT &amp; BEACON (T+15s – T+45s)
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="phase-body-grid">
          <div class="phase-info">
            <span class="badge badge-accent" id="phase-badge">PAD STANDBY &amp; HEALTH CHECK</span>
            <h3 id="phase-title" style="margin:0.5rem 0;">Pad Initialization &amp; 500-Sample Gyro Bias Zeroing</h3>
            <p id="phase-desc" class="body-copy">
              On the pad, the flight computer reads baseline barometric pressure P0 (MS5611), locks GPS fix (NEO-7M), and runs 500 stationary samples over 1.0s to compute IMU gyro/accel biases. The status LED glows Amber during calibration and turns Green when disarmed ready.
            </p>

            <div class="phase-telemetry-box mono">
              <div><span>ALTITUDE AGL:</span> <strong id="ph-alt">0.0 m</strong></div>
              <div><span>VELOCITY:</span> <strong id="ph-vel">0.0 m/s (Mach 0.0)</strong></div>
              <div><span>ACTIVE ACTUATOR:</span> <strong id="ph-act">Fins Locked at 90° (Disarmed)</strong></div>
              <div><span>PYRO STATUS:</span> <strong id="ph-pyro">All MOSFETs Gate Clamped to 0V (Safe)</strong></div>
              <div><span>WS2812 STATUS:</span> <strong id="ph-led" style="color:var(--green);">SOLID GREEN (Ready)</strong></div>
              <div><span>DOWNLINK:</span> <strong id="ph-rf">433 MHz LoRa Pad Beacon @ 1 Hz</strong></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="phase-visual">
            <div class="rocket-anim-box" id="rocket-anim-box">
              <div class="anim-sky">
                <div class="anim-cloud cloud-1"></div>
                <div class="anim-cloud cloud-2"></div>
              </div>
              <!-- Visual rocket container -->
              <div class="anim-rocket" id="anim-rocket-sprite">
                <div class="anim-nose"></div>
                <div class="anim-body">
                  <span class="anim-ignis-text mono">IGNIS</span>
                </div>
                <div class="anim-fins">
                  <div class="anim-fin fin-left" id="vis-fin-left"></div>
                  <div class="anim-fin fin-right" id="vis-fin-right"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="anim-flame" id="vis-flame"></div>
                <div class="anim-chute" id="vis-chute">🪂</div>
              </div>
              <div class="anim-ground"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
